lines_of_file.plain, line 1: Use "read" to get the lines in the file "todos.txt", or keep the text under a name first.

    set todos to the lines of "todos.txt"
                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    read the lines of "todos.txt" and call it todos
  or
    set my text to "todos.txt"
    set todos to the lines of my text
Why: "the lines of" splits the text "todos.txt" itself. To get what's in the file, Plain says "read".

lines_of_file.plain, line 2: Use "read" to get the words in the file "notes.txt", or keep the text under a name first.

    show the number of the words of "notes.txt"
                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    read "notes.txt" and call it notes
    show the number of the words of notes
  or
    set my text to "notes.txt"
    show the number of the words of my text
Why: "the words of" splits the text "notes.txt" itself. To get what's in the file, Plain says "read".

